<p>What matters just as much is the <strong>weakness</strong> Karpathy flagged: moving artifacts — games, worlds — are <strong>hard for an LLM to audit</strong>. Models cannot natively perceive video, so Opus 5 had to <strong>slowly, painstakingly take screenshots at different points</strong> to check its own scene, and it slipped a few times along the way — hence the jank. It can build the thing but <strong>cannot watch what it built</strong> — the most precise one-liner this experiment leaves behind.</p>

